# AI Optimize — Committed vs Ignored Policy
#
# Committed (portable repository metadata):
#   .ai-optimize/project.json       — Canonical project identity (schema version, projectId,
#                                      registeredRoot, aliases). Travels with the repo so that
#                                      every clone has the same stable identity.
#
# Generated derived state (committed — tracks with repo, regenerated on compile):
#   .ai-optimize/project-profile.json — Provider-neutral project profile.
#
# Local runtime state (NOT committed — machine-specific or ephemeral):
#   .ai-optimize/managed-artifacts.json — Activation ledger with machine-specific hashes and
#                                          absolute paths. NOT committed.
#   .ai-optimize/backups/               — Backup snapshots (ephemeral runtime state).
#   .ai-optimize/activation.lock        — Process lock (ephemeral).
#   .ai-optimize/events.jsonl           — Event history containing local activity timestamps.
#   .ai-optimize/*.db, *.db-wal, *.db-shm  — SQLite databases (local runtime state).
#   .ai-optimize/staging/               — Staging directory for activation.
#
# .ai-optimize/project.json is the single source of truth for stable project ID
# across all operations, migrations, and clones. It must be committed to ensure
# identity survives clones, branches, and CI environments.

# Ignored: local runtime state, backups, locks, databases, staging, temp files
.ai-optimize/backups/
.ai-optimize/activation.lock
.ai-optimize/managed-artifacts.json
.ai-optimize/events.jsonl
.ai-optimize/staging/
.ai-optimize/*.db
.ai-optimize/*.db-wal
.ai-optimize/*.db-shm

# OS Files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
